# Engineering Notes — {{CAMPAIGN_TITLE}}

The **append-only record of engineering "why" decisions** — the reasoning behind non-obvious choices, the
conditions each rests on, and what would make you revisit it. This is distinct from:
- **`CONVENTIONS.md`** — the *rules* themselves (sign conventions, units, naming); this holds *why* a rule
  was chosen.
- **the experiment `JOURNAL` / `logbook`** — *what happened* per experiment; this holds *why a choice was
  made*, which often spans experiments.

Where `record-decision` entries land. **Append-only:** never rewrite history — supersede an old entry with
a new one and link them. Record a decision when it is non-obvious and consequential and a future reader
would otherwise have to reverse-engineer it (a method/library/parameterization choice, an approximation a
result rests on, a non-obvious convention, an accepted trade-off, the *why* of a non-obvious verification
check). Skip the obvious.

> Each entry uses six fields: **decision · alternatives · why · provenance · conditions · revisit-if.**
> *Provenance* is **mandatory** — the source the decision is pinned to + confidence (PINNED / REPORTED /
> INFERRED / RECALLED, or REASONED for a pure-judgment call with no external fact). (Template + guidance:
> the `record-decision` skill.) **The source-authority ledger from campaign setup (`new-campaign` Step 0.6)
> seeds the first EDs here** — one per load-bearing fact resolved from a source.

