## Known landmines / Do-not-repeat
A short, scannable list of hard-won "never do this again" hazards — the things that broke the machine,
corrupted a run, or cost hours. Distinct from the ED rationale below: this is the fast **pre-flight
checklist**. **Re-check it before any action matching a listed trigger** (GPU use, launching a
detached/long process, overwriting inputs, …), and **proactively surface the relevant landmine to the user
before complying** with a request that would hit one — don't silently walk into it. A landmine that lives
only in a chat message or a memory file will not be re-checked (a real campaign re-triggered a
machine-freezing GPU path twice because the warning wasn't captured here).

| trigger (when about to…) | landmine (what went wrong) | do instead |
|---|---|---|
| <e.g. use the GPU for the dictionary build> | <froze the whole machine twice; hard reboot> | <use the CPU-parallel path; do NOT re-enable the GPU build> |

